is starting to work for us.

00:33:02.600 --> 00:33:05.450
And as we start to migrate
out, our customers asked,

00:33:05.450 --> 00:33:09.860
and that led to the formation
of 42Q in 2013 internally.

00:33:09.860 --> 00:33:13.690
And then we did the go-to-market
activities and we launched.

00:33:13.690 --> 00:33:15.770
The thing that's interesting
as you go through

00:33:15.770 --> 00:33:19.370
is, in order to enable people
to operate in the cloud,

00:33:19.370 --> 00:33:20.360
you need a gateway.

00:33:20.360 --> 00:33:23.930
And that's where, I think,
the role of Chrome and Android

00:33:23.930 --> 00:33:27.700
significantly propelled us
to get to the cloud segment.

00:33:31.180 --> 00:33:33.850
So moving forward,
how does this work?

00:33:33.850 --> 00:33:36.450
So you're buying product
from your customer.

00:33:36.450 --> 00:33:38.710
You expect the product,
when they come to you,

00:33:38.710 --> 00:33:41.890
to be very well designed, very
well tested, and completely

00:33:41.890 --> 00:33:43.570
fully functional.

00:33:43.570 --> 00:33:47.270
Every customer of 42Q
expects the same thing.

00:33:47.270 --> 00:33:51.550
So today, in the
cloud platform, we

00:33:51.550 --> 00:33:54.130
are getting over hundreds
of millions of widgets going

00:33:54.130 --> 00:33:56.260
through our platform today.

00:33:56.260 --> 00:33:59.759
Right, and that's the kind
of volume we are handling.

00:33:59.759 --> 00:34:02.050
And when you think about
that, when people are building

00:34:02.050 --> 00:34:04.300
a product in that kind
of volume and complexity,

00:34:04.300 --> 00:34:06.760
what's important
is the production

00:34:06.760 --> 00:34:10.120
supervisors want to make sure
that they are supplementing

00:34:10.120 --> 00:34:12.400
the operator capability
and the machine capability

00:34:12.400 --> 00:34:15.650
with automation that
will prevent mistakes.

00:34:15.650 --> 00:34:18.489
Right, simple example would be
if you're building a product

00:34:18.489 --> 00:34:21.509
and the testing shows you
that the product's kind

00:34:21.509 --> 00:34:23.800
of going to the tolerance
level, when you're out of it,

00:34:23.800 --> 00:34:26.080
it will automatically
stop the machine.

00:34:26.080 --> 00:34:28.870
So we do things like that,
what we call a forced quality

00:34:28.870 --> 00:34:32.020
framework, that allows
production supervisor to really

00:34:32.020 --> 00:34:33.489
manage the factory.

00:34:33.489 --> 00:34:35.560
So what are the key
questions they ask?

00:34:35.560 --> 00:34:38.139
Did I build the product
correct the first time?

00:34:38.139 --> 00:34:41.901
It's a simple question, but when
you look below that, what does

00:34:41.901 --> 00:34:43.400
"did they build it
correctly?" mean?

00:34:43.400 --> 00:34:45.010
Did the correct people touch it?

00:34:45.010 --> 00:34:46.899
So we have to track
every operator.

00:34:46.899 --> 00:34:49.080
So our Chrome and
Android devices

00:34:49.080 --> 00:34:50.530
where the operator
interacts with,

00:34:50.530 --> 00:34:51.730
we track the transactions.

00:34:51.730 --> 00:34:52.330
Who did it?

00:34:52.330 --> 00:34:53.020
What happened?

00:34:53.020 --> 00:34:53.739
When?

00:34:53.739 --> 00:34:56.469
The timestamping is
extremely critical.

00:34:56.469 --> 00:34:59.200
Right, so if you're building
an FDA class 3-- class 3,

00:34:59.200 --> 00:35:02.680
for people who don't know, is
it's intrusive into your body

00:35:02.680 --> 00:35:05.467
and people could die if
it's produced incorrectly.

00:35:05.467 --> 00:35:07.300
So when you're building
a product like that,

00:35:07.300 --> 00:35:10.610
timestamping and traceability
becomes so critical,

00:35:10.610 --> 00:35:13.330
and that's why we call it
the forced quality framework.

00:35:13.330 --> 00:35:15.820
Really, it ensures
that the right people

00:35:15.820 --> 00:35:17.080
touched the product.

00:35:17.080 --> 00:35:20.320
The machines were calibrated
and maintained correctly.

00:35:20.320 --> 00:35:23.080
The quality data was collected
and processed correctly

00:35:23.080 --> 00:35:24.910
so that the product
can be shipped.

00:35:24.910 --> 00:35:28.270
And lastly, we make sure that
with all of that information,

00:35:28.270 --> 00:35:30.670
there was management
oversight and approval

00:35:30.670 --> 00:35:32.870
to deliver the quality product.

00:35:32.870 --> 00:35:35.110
So that's really our
forced quality framework

00:35:35.110 --> 00:35:38.620
that allows our customers
to effectively use it.

00:35:38.620 --> 00:35:40.960
And with all of this
happening in the cloud,

00:35:40.960 --> 00:35:43.640
the gateway is generally a
Chrome device or an Android

00:35:43.640 --> 00:35:44.140
device.

00:35:47.660 --> 00:35:51.900
So let's talk about the
devices assets used.

00:35:51.900 --> 00:35:54.190
Typically, in a
factory floor, when

00:35:54.190 --> 00:35:55.990
somebody is building
a product, what

00:35:55.990 --> 00:35:58.600
happens is that, as
Rajen mentioned earlier,

00:35:58.600 --> 00:36:01.480
sales are sitting in the
front office taking orders.

00:36:01.480 --> 00:36:03.430
And invariably, it
happens that there will

00:36:03.430 --> 00:36:04.660
be a really critical order.

00:36:04.660 --> 00:36:06.244
Somebody wants to
follow through.

00:36:06.244 --> 00:36:08.410
You want to make sure you're
getting the right data.

00:36:08.410 --> 00:36:10.750
You want to make sure
that you are effectively

00:36:10.750 --> 00:36:14.050
delivering the product
to what you promised.

00:36:14.050 --> 00:36:16.960
And what happens in our
world is you can actually

00:36:16.960 --> 00:36:19.690
use a Chromebook or
an Android tablet,

00:36:19.690 --> 00:36:22.150
log in to the
application as a sales,

00:36:22.150 --> 00:36:25.330
export the data into G Suite,
share it with your production

00:36:25.330 --> 00:36:27.910
supervisor, and say, here
is kind of the five things

00:36:27.910 --> 00:36:28.750
that I want to do.

00:36:28.750 --> 00:36:31.480
Get me back in this so
I can share the more

00:36:31.480 --> 00:36:33.580
recent learnings
to the customer,

00:36:33.580 --> 00:36:35.380
or whatever the case might be.

00:36:35.380 --> 00:36:38.140
So what you're really doing is,
historically, what people do,

00:36:38.140 --> 00:36:41.020
they'll take a piece of
paper, walk over, take notes

00:36:41.020 --> 00:36:43.770
on what needs to be
captured, come back in,

00:36:43.770 --> 00:36:45.330
craft the email out.

00:36:45.330 --> 00:36:47.860
What you have done now, with
this kind of an environment,

00:36:47.860 --> 00:36:50.110
is that you've changed
the whole thing.

00:36:50.110 --> 00:36:54.040
First and foremost, you allowed
them to get access to data.

00:36:54.040 --> 00:36:55.600
Second is you allowed
them to take it

00:36:55.600 --> 00:36:58.220
to a collaborative
environment like G Suite that

00:36:58.220 --> 00:36:59.950
allows you to share
with the front office

00:36:59.950 --> 00:37:02.050
and effectively communicate.

00:37:02.050 --> 00:37:05.500
And that's really
the one part of that.

00:37:05.500 --> 00:37:07.450
The second piece
is, as I mentioned,

00:37:07.450 --> 00:37:09.640
factories have machines.

00:37:09.640 --> 00:37:11.950
The machines is an
interesting part.

00:37:11.950 --> 00:37:14.680
If you think about where
the world is going,

00:37:14.680 --> 00:37:18.040
the common theme
is industrial IOT.

00:37:18.040 --> 00:37:20.800
And everybody has heard
about industrial IOT,

00:37:20.800 --> 00:37:23.690
but I can tell you, industrial
IOT for manufacturing

00:37:23.690 --> 00:37:26.080
is progressing slowly.

00:37:26.080 --> 00:37:28.300
Part of the reason why
it's progressing slowly

00:37:28.300 --> 00:37:29.950
is the complexity.

00:37:29.950 --> 00:37:32.290
You heard about the
capabilities we deliver.

00:37:32.290 --> 00:37:35.140
Imagine, typically, in
an on-premise solution,

00:37:35.140 --> 00:37:37.040
when somebody buys
something like that,

00:37:37.040 --> 00:37:39.250
they're going to buy
roughly about anywhere

00:37:39.250 --> 00:37:43.150
from six to eight
servers, minimum, and up.

00:37:43.150 --> 00:37:44.310
You got to get them set up.

00:37:44.310 --> 00:37:45.250
You've got to configure them.

00:37:45.250 --> 00:37:46.833
You've got to get
them up and running.

00:37:46.833 --> 00:37:49.930
You got to install the
application, train the people.

00:37:49.930 --> 00:37:52.180
You don't need to do all
of that with the cloud.

00:37:52.180 --> 00:37:54.250
Similarly, when
machine connectivity,

00:37:54.250 --> 00:37:56.680
our view of the
world was, how do you

00:37:56.680 --> 00:37:58.450
make that complexity go away?

00:37:58.450 --> 00:38:01.330
How do you simplify
industrial IOT?

00:38:01.330 --> 00:38:05.540
So what we enable is there's two
kinds of models you can have--

00:38:05.540 --> 00:38:07.930
machines that can talk to
cloud, the newer machines

00:38:07.930 --> 00:38:09.090
are cloud-friendly.

00:38:09.090 --> 00:38:09.590
Great.

00:38:09.590 --> 00:38:11.500
You can use a standard
protocol, IOT protocol

00:38:11.500 --> 00:38:13.810
and connect to us like MQTT.

00:38:13.810 --> 00:38:17.990
Or you can use a Chrome
that can be on site, right,

00:38:17.990 --> 00:38:19.600
but it's still
local software-less.

00:38:19.600 --> 00:38:21.580
It's one environment
for everybody.

00:38:21.580 --> 00:38:25.090
It connects, talks to the cloud,
and assures you the local data

00:38:25.090 --> 00:38:26.590
integrity.

00:38:26.590 --> 00:38:28.360
So that's how we
connect the machines

00:38:28.360 --> 00:38:31.800
and enable IOT for
the open market.

00:38:31.800 --> 00:38:34.120
Lastly, you know, if you
think about the products

00:38:34.120 --> 00:38:35.500
that we build,
products can be as

00:38:35.500 --> 00:38:37.620
small as what we're
carrying in the hand,

00:38:37.620 --> 00:38:40.030
to some products that are
built by our customers that

00:38:40.030 --> 00:38:40.770
are really huge.

00:38:40.770 --> 00:38:43.900
They could be 16 feet
long, eight feet tall,

00:38:43.900 --> 00:38:46.750
and a really broad
equipment, size of a room.

00:38:46.750 --> 00:38:49.510
So you had to build a
solution that allows you

00:38:49.510 --> 00:38:51.520
to be able to balance the two.

00:38:51.520 --> 00:38:53.920
And so our Android
platform basically

00:38:53.920 --> 00:38:57.430
allows you to have a really
significant user interface

00:38:57.430 --> 00:39:00.160
that you can read from 10
feet, 12 feet, or 15 feet

00:39:00.160 --> 00:39:02.410
away, for operators
who are operating

00:39:02.410 --> 00:39:05.290
with really bulky products.

00:39:05.290 --> 00:39:08.740
It's a really tailored platform,
but uses the same framework.

00:39:08.740 --> 00:39:10.240
Everything's running
on the cloud,

00:39:10.240 --> 00:39:13.360
provides you with the ability
to communicate and collaborate

00:39:13.360 --> 00:39:15.270
with our back-end solution.

00:39:19.750 --> 00:39:22.140
If you've been to
a factory, you know

00:39:22.140 --> 00:39:24.840
digital signage has changed
the world of a factory.

00:39:24.840 --> 00:39:25.530
You're smiling.

00:39:25.530 --> 00:39:27.300
Is that a question?

00:39:27.300 --> 00:39:27.800
No?

00:39:27.800 --> 00:39:29.100
All right.

00:39:29.100 --> 00:39:31.350
Digital signage has changed
the world of the factory,

00:39:31.350 --> 00:39:33.120
because in the old
days, people used

00:39:33.120 --> 00:39:35.670
to put charts of quality
information in the factory.

00:39:35.670 --> 00:39:37.470
When you walk in,
you can see it.

00:39:37.470 --> 00:39:40.890
You'll see the Lean and the Six
Sigma and all the terms there.

00:39:40.890 --> 00:39:43.850
All that's gone away, and now
you have a digital signage

00:39:43.850 --> 00:39:44.900
solution.

00:39:44.900 --> 00:39:46.710
What's powerful about this?

00:39:46.710 --> 00:39:48.820
In the old days, you
could have a signage

00:39:48.820 --> 00:39:51.000
only inside the factory.

00:39:51.000 --> 00:39:54.210
With today's world, with our
solution running on the cloud,

00:39:54.210 --> 00:39:55.980
and with the Android
equipment that you

00:39:55.980 --> 00:39:58.650
can use for displaying
anywhere, we're

00:39:58.650 --> 00:40:00.630
able to enable digital signage.

00:40:00.630 --> 00:40:02.250
I could have a
corporate office here

00:40:02.250 --> 00:40:03.770
that has a signage
of my factory,

00:40:03.770 --> 00:40:06.750
as in this case, the
factories in Singapore.

00:40:06.750 --> 00:40:09.430
Not only that, this
signage actually,

00:40:09.430 --> 00:40:13.680
as he pointed out in the case of
the Coca-Cola, similarly here,

00:40:13.680 --> 00:40:16.690
our IOT platform enables you
to get real-time information

00:40:16.690 --> 00:40:19.020
of the machines, and
it shows you in red,

00:40:19.020 --> 00:40:21.870
green, yellow in
an easy visual form

00:40:21.870 --> 00:40:23.830
as to whether there's a problem.

00:40:23.830 --> 00:40:25.830
It also shows you,
if there's a problem,

00:40:25.830 --> 00:40:28.720
has somebody responded to it?

00:40:28.720 --> 00:40:30.390
And if you're an
executive traveling,

00:40:30.390 --> 00:40:32.760
you can get that on
your mobile device.

00:40:32.760 --> 00:40:34.650
Foundationally, all
of this is enabled

00:40:34.650 --> 00:40:37.890
by using one consistent
platform to deliver the content.

00:40:41.570 --> 00:40:43.580
The last use case I
want to leave you with

00:40:43.580 --> 00:40:46.280
is general operations
management.

00:40:46.280 --> 00:40:50.420
Now, we talked about,
if you think about where

00:40:50.420 --> 00:40:52.550
the world's going,
is cloud's become--

00:40:52.550 --> 00:40:55.700
from the start of the cloud,
we started with burst capacity,

00:40:55.700 --> 00:40:57.800
and now it's mainstream.

00:40:57.800 --> 00:40:59.780
Same thing for manufacturing.

00:40:59.780 --> 00:41:01.580
It's becoming mainstream.

00:41:01.580 --> 00:41:03.770
We don't need any more
hardware, software,

00:41:03.770 --> 00:41:07.730
anything to be run on premise
to get manufacturing connected.

00:41:07.730 --> 00:41:10.160
You can connect the front
office to the back office

00:41:10.160 --> 00:41:13.400
now with real-time
transparency so people

00:41:13.400 --> 00:41:15.860
are able to collaborate
and effectively respond

00:41:15.860 --> 00:41:17.900
to their customer demands.

00:41:17.900 --> 00:41:22.070
You're also able to easily
connect the factory machines

00:41:22.070 --> 00:41:23.810
to the back end.

00:41:23.810 --> 00:41:26.350
With the kind of volume
that's going through today

00:41:26.350 --> 00:41:28.700
in this platform, we
get data from machines,

00:41:28.700 --> 00:41:31.100
we get data from over
hundreds of millions

00:41:31.100 --> 00:41:33.350
of widgets that goes
out, effectively

00:41:33.350 --> 00:41:34.640
through our product.

00:41:34.640 --> 00:41:36.800
And all of this is
able to do it today

00:41:36.800 --> 00:41:39.380
because we don't have
to deal with putting

00:41:39.380 --> 00:41:42.560
an application that runs
a software on premise

00:41:42.560 --> 00:41:43.700
and doing a lot of things.

00:41:43.700 --> 00:41:48.170
And we use, basically, our
Android and Chrome platforms

00:41:48.170 --> 00:41:52.100
to be able to be literally
software-less on premise,

00:41:52.100 --> 00:41:53.840
and that's the power
of the devices that

00:41:53.840 --> 00:41:56.810
allows us to fundamentally
simplify and even

00:41:56.810 --> 00:41:59.030
enable industrial
IOT for manufacturing

00:41:59.030 --> 00:42:02.880
for a vast majority
of our customers.

